==Restrictions==
Max # of Deployable Cats: 15

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*4 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 56.67~63.33 seconds<sup>1,700f~1,900f</sup>.
*1 [[Cumulus Gallus]] spawns as the boss after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>.
*1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>.
*4 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 43.33~50 seconds<sup>1,300f~1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Due to both THE FOLIVOREAN's and Cumulus Gallus' high damage most units will die in one or two hits. Be aware of your cash during the stage, as none of the peons give a lot money, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] might be considered.

Disposable units like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] or [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime cat]] will do well here. Research [[Cat Combo|Cat Combos]] can be useful for making sure there are always some units on the field.

If possessed, an [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|A. Bahamut]] with the help of a few attack up [[CatCombo|combos]] and fast units can consistently knockback Cumulus Gallus and chain him to death before THE FOLIVOREAN can cause problems.

=='''Recommended Units'''==
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Does high damage to both of the main threats and can deal with Wild Doge.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] - Kills the Wild and Aku doges and uses them as stepping stones to chip Condemned Peng and Cumulus. After the latter is dead, can also help chip FOLIVOREAN.
*[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] - Fast and tanky. Can stall both FOLIVOREAN and Cumulus (as long as his strengthen is not active).
*[[Cat Cactus]] - Can tank a lot of hits from the aku enemies here, but can be easily killed by strengthened Cumulus.

